Recommended video concept

Title / angle
Teens Are Officially Over Brainrot

Core message
After years of irony, overstimulation, and nonsense memes, teens are swinging back toward nostalgia, real hobbies, and turning ordinary life into the vibe.

Why this is the best one
It pulls together the most durable themes from the page:

anti-brainrot / meme reset
nostalgia for “simpler” internet culture
analogue / offline hobbies
everyday-life-as-cinema edits

It’s also much easier to build with stock than something slang-specific or challenge-specific, because slang ages fast and dance trends need exact audio/context. This concept can still feel current in a week, a month, or even longer.

Best format

Vertical 9:16
Length: 30–40 seconds
Style: fast hook, then warm nostalgic payoff
Pacing: first 5 seconds chaotic, next 20 seconds calming and affirming, last 5–10 seconds punchy close

Stock footage you’ll need

Use clips like these:

Teen scrolling phone in dark room
Fast flashing screens / glitchy social media feeling
Teen looking overwhelmed or bored
Close-up of phone being set face down
Friends riding bikes / walking outside
Teen journaling or writing in notebook
Physical books, sketching, polaroids, camcorder, CD player, cassette, record player
Friends laughing in kitchen / bedroom / school hallway
Making a snack or pouring cereal dramatically
Sunlight through bedroom window
Mirror outfit shot / simple glow-up moment
Group hanging out with no phones visible
Final warm “main character” walking shot

If you can find footage with a slightly nostalgic grade already baked in, even better.

Editing style

Open with overstimulating cuts for 3–5 seconds:
zooms
glitch
motion blur
notification sounds
harsh contrast

Then hard-switch into:
warmer tones
film grain
slower cuts
gentle handheld feel
soft light leaks if available

That visual transition is the whole point of the video.

